# Non-secret config baked into the release BUNDLE from GitHub variables.
#
# Written by .github/workflows/release.yml immediately before the image build,
# from repository-level `vars.*`, and carried to every host inside
# /deploy-bundle. GitHub is the source of truth; the agent pulls it rather than
# CI pushing it, so nothing in GitHub can reach a server.
#
# Committed EMPTY on purpose. It must exist for `docker compose` to resolve the
# env_file from a plain checkout (local dev, the CI smoke test), and it must
# never carry a real value into git — the workflow overwrites the working copy
# and does not commit it.
#
# ── This file is a DEFAULT, not the last word ───────────────────────────────
#
# Every service lists it BEFORE server.env, and compose gives the later file
# precedence. So /etc/hqcat/<stack>/server.env still overrides anything here,
# which is what makes one shared image serve two stacks: values that differ
# per stack (APNS_ENV on a sandbox build, say) are set on the host and win.
#
# SECRETS DO NOT BELONG HERE. This file is inside the image, readable by anyone
# who can pull it. Secrets live in /etc/hqcat/<stack>/secrets/ and reach the
# container as compose `secrets:` via the *_FILE convention.
